{"type":"research","references":[{"note":"Host Haru-san is a small, slightly plump adult man with short silver hair in a low bun, round tortoiseshell glasses, wearing a mustard-yellow knit cardigan over a white blouse, navy apron, beige long skirt, and brown slip-on shoes.","url":"https://deeptokyo.jp/en/food_gourmet/1588","title":"Experiencing the Charm of Traditional Japanese Kissaten and the Showa Era｜DEEPTOKYOmagazine","use":"costume"},{"note":"The kissaten interior features a wooden counter, siphon coffee maker, teapots, old tube radio, round wall clock, potted plants, and a large window letting in warm afternoon light; main color #efe2c6, accent #b0773a.","url":"https://deeptokyo.jp/en/food_gourmet/1588","title":"Experiencing the Charm of Traditional Japanese Kissaten and the Showa Era｜DEEPTOKYOmagazine","use":"set"},{"note":"Palette of warm amber, cream, and muted sage includes #efe2c6 (main), #b0773a (accent), #d9a63a (cardigan), #8fa58a (sage), #2f3d5c (apron and accent).","url":"https://deeptokyo.jp/en/food_gourmet/1588","title":"Experiencing the Charm of Traditional Japanese Kissaten and the Showa Era｜DEEPTOKYOmagazine","use":"palette"},{"note":"A faded old envelope on the counter is described as an insert from fifty years ago, containing a letter that could not be sent to a loved one.","url":"https://www.haniseoul.com/travels/japan/kissaten-retro-cafe-tokyo","title":"Kissaten Guide: Encountering Showa Era Nostalgia in Tokyo's Retro Cafes | HaniSeoul","use":"props"},{"note":"An elderly gentleman enters carrying an old envelope; the door makes a 'カラン' sound as it opens.","url":"https://www.haniseoul.com/travels/japan/kissaten-retro-cafe-tokyo","title":"Kissaten Guide: Encountering Showa Era Nostalgia in Tokyo's Retro Cafes | HaniSeoul","use":"customs"},{"note":"The veranda (縁側) of the kissaten is part of the set, extending the warm, nostalgic atmosphere with the same color scheme.","url":"https://deeptokyo.jp/en/food_gourmet/1588","title":"Experiencing the Charm of Traditional Japanese Kissaten and the Showa Era｜DEEPTOKYOmagazine","use":"set"}]}
