{"type":"plan","title":"ひだまり人生劇場・春の手紙","logline":"五十年越しの想いが、桜の香りと共に解き放たれる午後","shots":[{"index":1,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"The kissaten interior basks in spring afternoon light. Warm sunbeams stream through the large window onto the wooden counter, teapots, and potted plants. Cream walls glow amber. Haru-san stands behind the counter, wiping a cup.","mode":"still","dialogue":"春の午後、喫茶ひだまりの窓から、やわらかな日が差しこみます。","cites":[1,2,3]},{"index":2,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"The wooden door slides open with a gentle 'karan' chime. The elderly gentleman steps inside, stooped slightly, dark navy coat catching the light. He clutches the yellowed envelope in both hands, eyes scanning the room.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"カランと扉が鳴って、古い封筒を手にした、老紳士が入ってきました。","cites":[5]},{"index":3,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Insert shot: the envelope rests on the wooden counter, its frayed corners and dark amber wax stamp catching the afternoon sun. Dust motes drift in the beam. The seal is intact, fifty years of silence held in paper fibers.","mode":"still","dialogue":"五十年前、好きだった人に、出せなかった手紙だといいます。","cites":[4]},{"index":4,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Over-the-shoulder from behind Haru-san as she pours cherry-blossom tea from a ceramic pot into two cups. Steam curls. She sets the pot down, turns, and sits on the stool beside the gentleman. Two-shot: both at the counter, tea between them.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"ハルさんは、桜の香りの紅茶を淹れて、黙って、となりに座りました。","cites":[1,2]},{"index":5,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"The gentleman lifts the envelope, breaks the wax seal, and unfolds the letter. He reads aloud, voice low. Haru listens, hands on her cup. Light slants lower, amber deepening. He finishes, refolds, and a small smile crinkles his eyes.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"老紳士は、手紙を、声に出して読みはじめました。読み終えると、小さく、笑いました。","cites":[5]},{"index":6,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Tight on the gentleman's face, afternoon light gilding his cheekbones. Eyes glisten, smile lines deepen. He whispers the line to himself, shoulders dropping a lifetime's weight.","mode":"still","dialogue":"「やっと、言えた気がします」。","cites":[]},{"index":7,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Evening on the river path. Cherry trees in full bloom canopy the walkway, petals sailing on the breeze. The gentleman walks away from us, envelope in hand. A single petal spirals down and lands on the flap. Amber-gold water reflects blossoms.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"帰り道、川沿いの桜が、ひとひら、封筒の上に落ちました。","cites":[]}]}
